' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/claims/application/claim.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Claimant / Finder" as Actor
participant "Private Conversation" as Page
participant "Claims API" as API
participant "Claim Chat Service" as Service
participant "claim_evidence" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open View protected claim evidence
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: GET /api/claims/:id/evidence/:evidenceId
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: View protected claim evidence
activate Service
Service -> Table: 5: SELECT claim-scoped private evidence
activate Table
Table --> Service: 6: Evidence storage metadata
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 7: Require actual room participant; never role-only Staff access
alt Business rules satisfied
Service -> Service: 8: Resolve private asset through storage adapter; stream bytes
Service --> API: 9: Protected image bytes
API --> Page: 10: HTTP 200: Protected image bytes
Page --> Actor: 11: Render evidence preview without exposing raw storage reference
else Missing or ineligible context
Service --> API: 8.1: No authorized evidence for this room
API --> Page: 8.2: HTTP 404
Page --> Actor: 8.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Related tables, authorization, transactions and audit remain inside the service. Catalogue status is
not deployment or manual acceptance.
endlegend
